     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those need a foothold there, which can only come from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup. Each of these requires stolen_dbadmin AND (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). mfa:dbadmin is deployed, so the attacker would need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those come only from escalate_dc or escalate_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. The only way to get those is auth_dc or auth_adfs, which require NOT mfa_admin, and mfa:admin is deployed. So admin_dc and admin_adfs are unreachable. The attacker can still get stolen_dbadmin (via phish, pivot, auth_ciserver, escalate_ciserver, leak_secrets_ciserver) and reach_internal, but cannot authenticate to db, fileserver or backup. Exfiltration is unreachable.\"}\n```"
